/-!
# Non-characteristic-two branches of the rank-two component argument

The explicit (4,3)-partition stabilizer has a normal three-group, contradicting
local characteristic two. The terminal reduction retains the actual component
centralizer quotient, forces case (2) of Hypothesis 15.3.10 from an order-four
commutator, and proves the chain giving L ≤ M from the model fixer calculation.

The A₇ placement, the exclusions in case (e) of 1.1.5(3), the sporadic local
sieve leaving Aut(J₂), and the actual J₂ action calculations remain outstanding.
No complete source-numbered 15.3.42 theorem is asserted by this module.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript, printed p.1138.
-/
